  ('23cdaffa-189f-55cd-a6cc-190d49467cf6', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'rational-radical-expressions'), null, 'hard',
   $qq$For $x \neq -2$, rewrite $\dfrac{3x - 1}{x + 2}$ in the form $q + \dfrac{r}{x + 2}$, where $q$ and $r$ are numbers. Which is it?$qq$, $q$[{"text":"$3 - \\dfrac{3}{x + 2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-multiply-constant-by-quotient"},{"text":"$3 + \\dfrac{5}{x + 2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-instead-of-subtracted"},{"text":"$3 - \\dfrac{7}{x + 2}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$3 - \\dfrac{1}{x + 2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-adjust-constant"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$3 - \dfrac{7}{x + 2}$$q$, $q$Make the numerator look like a multiple of $x + 2$: $3(x + 2) = 3x + 6$, so $3x - 1 = 3(x + 2) - 7$. Then $\dfrac{3x - 1}{x + 2} = 3 - \dfrac{7}{x + 2}$. Check at $x = 0$: the original is $-\frac{1}{2}$ and $3 - \frac{7}{2} = -\frac{1}{2}$. The choice $3 + \dfrac{5}{x + 2}$ computes $-1 + 6$ instead of $-1 - 6$.$q$, 'draft', null)
