  ('be9377b8-dfc0-5a24-a24d-2424469b28d6', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'rational-radical-expressions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Simplify the complex fraction (for $x \neq 0$, $x \neq 1$ and $x \neq -1$): $\dfrac{1 + \frac{1}{x}}{1 - \frac{1}{x^2}}$. Which expression is the result?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\dfrac{(x + 1)^2(x - 1)}{x^3}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"multiplied-instead-of-dividing"},{"text":"$\\dfrac{x}{x + 1}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"canceled-wrong-factor"},{"text":"$\\dfrac{x}{x - 1}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\dfrac{1}{x - 1}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-x-instead-of-x-squared-denominator"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\dfrac{x}{x - 1}$$q$, $q$Write the top as $\dfrac{x + 1}{x}$ and the bottom as $\dfrac{x^2 - 1}{x^2} = \dfrac{(x - 1)(x + 1)}{x^2}$. Dividing means multiplying by the reciprocal: $\dfrac{x + 1}{x} \cdot \dfrac{x^2}{(x - 1)(x + 1)} = \dfrac{x}{x - 1}$. The choice $\dfrac{(x + 1)^2(x - 1)}{x^3}$ multiplies the two fractions instead of dividing.$q$, 'draft', null)
