   $q$Subtract (for $x \neq 2$ and $x \neq -2$): $\dfrac{x}{x^2 - 4} - \dfrac{1}{x - 2}$. Which expression is the result?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\dfrac{2}{x^2 - 4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-distribute-subtraction"},{"text":"$\\dfrac{x - 1}{x^2 - 4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-rescale-numerators"},{"text":"$\\dfrac{x - 1}{x^2 - x - 2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-denominators"},{"text":"$-\\dfrac{2}{x^2 - 4}$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$-\dfrac{2}{x^2 - 4}$$q$, $q$Since $x^2 - 4 = (x - 2)(x + 2)$, rewrite the second fraction as $\dfrac{x + 2}{x^2 - 4}$. Then subtract numerators: $x - (x + 2) = -2$, giving $-\dfrac{2}{x^2 - 4}$. The choice $\dfrac{2}{x^2 - 4}$ computes $x - x + 2$, forgetting that the minus sign applies to the whole $x + 2$.$q$, 'draft', null)
